why: the last gap of the microservices audit. specs/obs.md says
  outright "logging framework integration — log lines are not this
  spec's", and 51 printlns in main sources are what stands in for it.
  A log line nobody can join to a trace is a log line nobody reads
  during an incident.

what: okay-obs Log — a Line VALUE with a Schema (level, message,
  fields, traceId, spanId, at, logger); the program side is the
  core's own Writer effect (tell(line) — no new signature); the
  correlation is the HANDLER's, stamped from the ambient Tracer at
  write time, so programs stay observability-blind (obs.md's own
  doctrine). Handlers: console (one JSON object per line, what every
  collector reads), topic (the span treatment), collecting (tests).
  Tracer gains a public `context`.

